adm.manual.monitor_tools.storage_cell_title=Advanced Storage Link Cell
adm.manual.monitor_tools.link_scanner_title=Advance Link Scanner
adm.manual.item.advance_link_scanner=Scans loaded chunks for AdvanceDataMonitor link blocks (monitors, network/storage/crafting linkers).\n\nShift+right-click: scan all loaded chunks. Stores results as an expandable list with owner names, coordinates, aliases, and block types.\n\nRight-click: open scanner GUI — browse entries, filter by owner/name, set custom aliases, and teleport directly to any found block.\n\nFilters: Owner (All/Mine/Others), Name (All/Unnamed/Named).\n\nTeleport: click a row to teleport to that block (same dimension, safe landing check).\n\nStack size: 1. Creative tab: Tools.

adm.manual.dimensional_pocket.overview_title=Dimensional Pocket Overview
adm.manual.dimensional_pocket.overview_text=The Dimensional Pocket is a player-UUID-bound portable storage. All pocket items in your inventory share the same storage space — the item itself carries no data.\n\nStorage persists across sessions in textech/pocket-<uuid>.dat inside the world save directory. Right-click opens the storage GUI; shift+right-click toggles the draggable overlay window.\n\nUpgrades: four types of upgrade cards expand capacity, add pages, multiply stack limits, and unlock infinite stacking. Cards are consumed on installation and cannot be recovered — except cards rejected by prerequisite rules.\n\nCapacity formula: slots per page = min(63, 1 + min(space upgrades, 62)); pages = 1 + min(page upgrades, 8) when space >= 64, else 1.

adm.manual.dimensional_pocket.pocket_title=Dimensional Pocket
adm.manual.dimensional_pocket.space_card_title=Space Upgrade Card
adm.manual.dimensional_pocket.page_card_title=Page Upgrade Card
adm.manual.dimensional_pocket.stack_card_title=Stack Upgrade Card
adm.manual.dimensional_pocket.infinite_stack_card_title=Infinite Stack Upgrade Card
adm.manual.dimensional_pocket.usage_title=Pocket Usage & Upgrade Rules
adm.manual.dimensional_pocket.usage_text=Storage GUI: right-click the pocket item. Top grid shows the current page; bottom shows player inventory. Drag or shift-click items between them. Use Prev/Next buttons to switch pages; Upgrade Config button opens the upgrade GUI.\n\nOverlay window: shift+right-click to toggle. A draggable pocket panel appears over any open container. AE2 containers auto-degrade to read-only when the overlay is active.\n\nUpgrade installation order: Space upgrades first (up to 64, baseline 1 slot) → Page upgrades (require 64 space upgrades, up to 8) → Stack upgrades (doubles per-slot stack limit, up to 8) → Infinite Stack upgrade (requires full stack upgrades, max 1).\n\nCards are consumed on install. Only cards rejected by prerequisite rules (e.g. page card before space is full) are returned to inventory.\n\nStack limit formula: base 64 × 2^n where n = stack upgrade count (max 10). Infinite card sets limit to Integer.MAX_VALUE.

adm.manual.item.dimensional_pocket=A player-UUID-bound portable storage pocket. All copies share the same storage.\n\nRight-click: open storage GUI with pocket grid + player inventory. Drag/shift-click items to transfer.\n\nShift+right-click: toggle overlay window (draggable, works over any container).\n\nStorage is per-player, persisted to world save/textech/pocket-<uuid>.dat.\n\nStack size: 1. Creative tab: Tools.

adm.manual.item.space_upgrade_card=Increases pocket slot capacity. Each card adds 1 slot (baseline 1, max 63 per page).\n\nStacks up to 64, but only 62 are effective for slots. Cards 63-64 unlock page upgrades.\n\nInstall via the Upgrade Config GUI (from storage GUI). Cards are consumed on installation.\n\nCreative tab: Tools.

adm.manual.item.page_upgrade_card=Adds extra pages to the pocket. Each card adds 1 page (max 8 = 9 pages total).\n\nRequires space upgrades to be fully stacked (64) to take effect.\n\nInstall via the Upgrade Config GUI. Cards are consumed on installation.\n\nCreative tab: Tools.

adm.manual.item.stack_upgrade_card=Doubles the per-slot stack limit. Base 64, formula: 64 × 2^n.\n\nScaling: 1=128, 2=256, 4=1024, 8=8192. Max 8 cards.\n\nInstall via the Upgrade Config GUI. Cards are consumed on installation.\n\nCreative tab: Tools.

adm.manual.item.infinite_stack_upgrade_card=Sets per-slot stack limit to Integer.MAX_VALUE for unlimited stacking.\n\nRequires stack upgrades to be full before taking effect. Max 1 card.\n\nWarning: very large stacks may cause rendering lag.\n\nInstall via the Upgrade Config GUI. Card is consumed on installation.\n\nCreative tab: Tools.

adm.manual.data_loom_cells.overview_title=Data Loom Cells — Lore & Overview
adm.manual.data_loom_cells.overview_text=AE digitizes matter into network data. AdvanceDataMonitor researchers reversed this — weaving data back into matter.\n\nEvolution:\n- Data Dust Loom Cell (basic): immature tech, only weaves the simplest form — dusts (GT dust prefix).\n- Data Form Loom Cell (advanced): full mastery, reconstructs any complex item.\n- Data Flow Cell: fluid channel, weaves data into fluids (mB units, default 1000 mB/s = 1 bucket/s).\n- Data Tide Loom Cell (advanced): fluid channel upgrade — tides of data, up to 63 fluid types.\n- Data Source Loom Cell: fluid channel, weaves data into Thaumcraft essentia (aspect fluids, default 1000 mB/s).\n\nUsage: place in ME Drive or ME Chest, mark targets in Cell Workbench, generate slowly over time. Dust/Form/Flow cells cannot mark AdvanceDataMonitor items. Output settles on a configurable interval (default 5 s); effective rates are cached on the item tooltip when markers or amplifier cards change. Weave Amplifier cards multiply output (default 4×/card, Super 16×/card, max 8 cards, multiplicative). Drains AE network energy.\n\nAdvanced Storage Linker note: contents stored inside Data Loom cells are excluded from Advanced Storage Linker statistics.\n\nConfig: [dataDustLoomCell], [dataFormLoomCell], [dataFlowCell], [dataSourceLoomCell], [dataLoomCell] (sync interval, energy drain, amplifier multipliers).

adm.manual.data_loom_cells.data_dust_loom_title=Data Dust Loom Cell
adm.manual.data_loom_cells.data_form_loom_title=Data Form Loom Cell
adm.manual.data_loom_cells.data_flow_cell_title=Data Flow / Tide Loom Cell
adm.manual.data_loom_cells.data_source_loom_title=Data Source Loom Cell
adm.manual.data_loom_cells.weave_amplifier_title=Weave Amplifier Cards
adm.manual.data_loom_cells.usage_title=Usage & Amplifier Installation
adm.manual.data_loom_cells.usage_text=How to use Data Loom Cells:\n\n1. Craft the desired cell type (Dust/Form/Flow/Tide/Source).\n2. Place the cell in a Cell Workbench. Mark target items/fluids/essentia in the partition slots.\n3. Optionally install Weave Amplifier or Super Weave Amplifier cards (max 8 combined). Only these cards are accepted — AE acceleration cards will not work.\n4. Insert the cell into an ME Drive or ME Chest (item channel for Dust/Form; fluid channel for Flow/Tide/Source).\n5. The cell automatically starts weaving — output settles every [dataLoomCell] syncIntervalSeconds (default 5s).\n\nAmplifier scaling:\n- Normal: 4× per card, multiplicative. 1→4×, 2→16×, 4→256×, 8→65536×.\n- Super: 16× per card, stacks multiplicatively with normal cards.\n- Max 8 cards shared across all types.\n\nEnergy: drains [dataLoomCell] energyDrainPerTick AE/t (default 999999).\n\nExternal access: internal accumulators can be read via storage bus, but are excluded from Advanced Storage Linker statistics.

adm.manual.grapple_system.overview_title=Grapple System Overview
adm.manual.grapple_system.overview_text=The Grapple System lets you travel through your beautifully built base with a sense of journey — enjoying the scenery instead of skipping it with teleport or flight.\n\nTwo components work together:\n- Grapple Anchor: face-mountable thin-plate nodes placed along paths.\n- Grapple Hook: handheld tool for attaching to and gliding between anchors.\n\nCore loop: approach anchor → magnetic-select with hook → right-click attach → look at next anchor → right-click glide → Shift to detach. Both hands remain free during travel.\n\nConfig: [grapple] category (hint range, interact distance, travel speed, magnetic angle). See Player Guide §3.7–3.8 for full usage details.

adm.manual.grapple_system.anchor_title=Grapple Anchor
adm.manual.grapple_system.hook_title=Grapple Hook
adm.manual.grapple_system.story_title=Design Intent & Quick Reference
adm.manual.grapple_system.story_text=We often spend enormous effort making beautiful bases and production lines, yet daily travel still defaults to flying, sprinting, or teleporting — flying and sprinting tie up your hands, and teleporting skips the scenery entirely.\n\nGrapple anchors and the grapple hook aim for a balance between "getting there fast" and "seeing the journey": place nodes along factory corridors, scenic bridges, production tour routes, and other key paths. Attach with the hook and glide smoothly between nodes while keeping both hands free — movement itself becomes part of the experience.\n\nQuick reference:\n- Grapple Anchor: wall/ceiling/floor mount, renameable, custom nav icon color\n- Grapple Hook: HUD hint within 12 blocks, magnetic attach within 6; shows reachable nodes through walls when attached\n- Right-click to attach, right-click again to travel, Shift to detach\n- Config category [grapple] (hint range, interact distance, travel speed, etc.)

adm.manual.combat_special.overview_title=Combat & Special Items Overview
adm.manual.combat_special.overview_text=AdvanceDataMonitor includes two legendary-tier combat/special items: the Empyrean Holy Judgment sword and the Super Orange utility item.\n\nThe Empyrean Holy Judgment is devastating in combat with instant-kill, slash waves, thrown attacks, and area sword rains. It also features cosmic shader rendering.\n\nThe Super Orange is a legendary utility item granting instant mining, matter ball conversion, companion drones, and projectile immunity — with deep config customization.\n\nBoth items are endgame-tier: the Super Orange drops from dungeon chests (0.1%) and mob kills (0.05%); the sword is crafted or given via creative mode.

adm.manual.combat_special.sword_title=Empyrean Holy Judgment
adm.manual.combat_special.orange_title=Super Orange
adm.manual.combat_special.usage_title=Combat & Ability Usage
adm.manual.combat_special.usage_text=Empyrean Holy Judgment (starry_cosmos_sword):\n- Left-click: instant kill + crescent slash wave\n- Right-click: throw straight along crosshair; 5-second sword rain on impact\n- Shift+right-click: mini judgment swords on mobs in 3×3 chunks\n- Cosmic shader rendering with custom particle effects\n\nSuper Orange (orange):\n- Hold: instant break any block (including GT ores)\n- Right-click: toggle drone and projectile immunity\n- Sneak+right-click: open settings GUI (nameplate, matter-ball / pickup / drop merge, drop multiplier)\n- Drone: orbits player, intercepts projectiles, clones fight hostiles\n\nSee Config Reference for [superOrange] and [dataLoomCell] categories.

adm.manual.item.starry_cosmos_sword=The ultimate combat weapon. Instant-kill left-click with crescent slash wave.\n\nLeft-click: kill target instantly, releasing a wide crescent slash wave in front.\n\nRight-click: throw the sword along your crosshair. On impact, triggers a 5-second sword rain over the area.\n\nShift+right-click: mini judgment swords rain on all hostile mobs within a 3×3 chunk area.\n\nCosmic rendering: uses special shader effects for a celestial appearance.\n\nCreative tab: Combat. Stack size: 1.
adm.manual.item.holy_judgment=Holy Judgment is the non-enchanted variant with the same skills.\n\nLeft-click giant stab and right-click throw/slam/rain: 10 true damage each (not instant kill).\n\nMelee and Shift+right-click mini swords: 5 true + 5 armor-respecting damage.\n\nSame cosmic rendering as Empyrean Holy Judgment (rain shows blade only for performance), without enchantment glow.\n\nRegistry: holy_judgment. Creative tab: Combat.

adm.manual.ai_assistant.teleport_title=Teleport System
adm.manual.ai_assistant.teleport_text=The AI Assistant integrates with Draconic Evolution's Advanced Dislocator (com.brandon3055.draconicevolution.common.items.tools.TeleporterMKII) for teleportation.\n\nRequirements:\n- An Advanced Dislocator (TeleporterMKII) in your inventory.\n- At least one saved destination on the gem (added via DE's own interface).\n\nHow it works:\n1. The assistant scans your inventory for TeleporterMKII items.\n2. Reads the "Locations" NBT tag list from each gem.\n3. Each location has: X, Y, Z, Dimension, Name.\n4. Displays destinations as a numbered list with dimension info.\n5. Confirm by number or fuzzy name match.\n\nExecution:\n- Same dimension: setPositionAndUpdate() for instant teleport.\n- Cross-dimension: uses configurationManager.transferPlayerToDimension() with a custom Teleporter instance.\n\nDimensions are resolved by stored DimentionName (DE uses this typo internally), standard names (Nether/Overworld/The End), or custom dimension IDs.\n\nName matching: exact match preferred, falls back to substring matching if no exact match found.\n\nExample AI prompts: "Teleport me to my base", "List my teleport points", "Take me to the mining dimension".

adm.manual.ai_assistant.planner_title=Planner Integration
adm.manual.ai_assistant.planner_text=The AI Assistant can manage your Advance Planner entries directly through text commands — no need to open the planner GUI for basic operations.\n\nSupported planner commands through AI:\n- "Add plan: build fusion reactor" — creates a new planner entry\n- "List my plans" — shows all current entries with their status\n- "Complete plan 1" — marks entry #1 as done\n- "Delete plan 2" — removes entry #2\n- "Modify plan 3 to say: build HV array" — updates entry text\n\nThis works from anywhere — the AI communicates with the server to modify the planner item in your inventory. The planner's NBT data is updated automatically.\n\nSee the Advance Planner chapter for full planner GUI usage, merging, HUD customization, and advanced features.

adm.manual.planner.overview_title=Advance Planner Overview
adm.manual.planner.overview_text=The Advance Planner is your personal task management tool with full NBT persistence. Store multiple todo entries, mark them complete, merge planners together, and optionally show a HUD overlay on screen.\n\nCore features:\n- Multiple entries per item with auto-numbering\n- Text + completed flag + creation timestamp per entry\n- Scrollable GUI (up to 50 visible rows)\n- Merge multiple planners into one (by time or by index)\n- On-screen HUD overlay with customizable position, scale, and width\n\nRight-click the planner item to open its GUI. Sneak+right-click to toggle the HUD. Press P to open from hotbar.\n\nThe planner also integrates with the AI Assistant — manage entries via natural language commands.

adm.manual.planner.item_title=Advance Planner
adm.manual.planner.entries_title=Entry Management
adm.manual.planner.entries_text=Each planner entry stores four fields in NBT:\n- slotIndex: auto-incrementing number (1, 2, 3...). Auto-renumbers on deletion.\n- text: the task description text you entered.\n- timestamp: creation time (System.currentTimeMillis(), displayed as yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm).\n- completed: boolean flag, toggleable via checkbox.\n\nCreating entries: click + or empty slot → type text → Enter. Editing: click text → edit → Enter. Toggle complete: click checkbox. Delete: trash icon. Reorder: up/top arrows.\n\nPersistence: all entries are stored in the item's NBT under the "plannerEntries" tag list. Data survives logout/login, item transfers, duplication, breaking and pickup.\n\nStats display: "Total N | Done N | Pending N" at the top of the planner GUI.

adm.manual.planner.merge_title=Planner Merging
adm.manual.planner.merge_text=When you have multiple planner items (e.g. from other players, creative mode, or accidental duplication), merge them into one:\n\n1. Open any planner GUI.\n2. Click Merge. The mod scans your inventory for all planner items.\n3. A merge confirmation window appears showing: "Found N planners with M total entries to merge".\n4. Choose merge mode:\n   By Time - sorts all entries by creation timestamp, newest first.\n   By Index - preserves original slot order from each planner, appending sequentially.\n5. Click Confirm Merge. A new merged ItemStack is created. Original items are consumed (except the opened one).\n\nThe merged planner gets a new nextSlotIndex, renumbering all entries sequentially.\n\nThis function uses mergePlanners() / mergeMultiplePlanners() static methods on ItemAdvancePlanner.

adm.manual.planner.hud_title=HUD Configuration
adm.manual.planner.hud_text=The HUD overlay displays planner entries on screen while playing. Full customization:\n\nHUD Config (accessible from planner GUI):\n- Max Display: number of entries shown (1-20, default 5).\n- Pos X/Y: normalized screen position (0.0=left/top, 1.0=right/bottom, default 1.0/0.0 = top-right).\n- Scale: size multiplier (0.5-3.0, default 1.0).\n- Width: text area width in pixels (80-600, default 160).\n- Custom Title: optional header text (empty = no title).\n\nPreview window: shows HUD position and size in real-time. Scroll wheel adjusts scale, Shift+scroll adjusts width.\n\nAll HUD settings are stored per-planner in the item's NBT. Different planner items can have completely different HUD configs.\n\nRange limits enforced by Config.java: plannerHudMin/Max values for each setting.\n\nHUD rendering uses HudRenderUtil for background, text wrapping, positioning, and scaling calculations.

