adm.manual.web_console.refresh_multi_title=Refresh & Multi-network
adm.manual.web_console.refresh_multi_text=Phase 1 introduced a throttled refresh model and multi-network display.\n\nRefresh model:\n- The server collects snapshots every refreshIntervalMs (default 1000 ms), spread across ticks so each tick only enqueues a bounded number of collection tasks (only networks active in the last 2 minutes are collected).\n- GT machines are collected every gtRefreshIntervalMs (default 10000 ms) on the same scheduler.\n- Power (EU/steam) keeps its 5-second sampling window; reads always go through the cache.\n- The browser only reads the cache (GET /api/storage, /api/power, /api/gt/machines). When the cache is empty it returns the last snapshot with cached:false until the scheduler catches up.\n- Auto-refresh polls at refreshIntervalMs and covers the current tab's data (storage/power/gt/orders).\n- Manual force-refresh is admin-only: POST /api/refresh (returns 403 for non-OP) or /admweb refresh [network] in-game.\n- A public /api/config endpoint returns refreshIntervalMs / gtRefreshIntervalMs / maxNetworksDisplayed / tokenLifetimeHours / themePresets so the frontend can adapt.\n\nMulti-network display:\n- The top bar network selector is a multi-select dropdown capped at maxNetworksDisplayed (default 5).\n- Split mode: each selected network renders its own cards/tables.\n- Merged mode: item amounts, fluids, essentia, bytes, EU/steam and machine counts are summed across selected networks (aggregation done in the browser).\n- Batch endpoints: GET /api/storage/batch?networks=0,1,2, POST /api/refresh/batch (admin), and equivalent /api/power/batch, /api/gt/machines/batch.
adm.manual.chapter.web_console=Web Console
adm.manual.web_console.brief_overview_title=WebAE Console
adm.manual.web_console.brief_overview_text=WebAE is TeXTech's embedded browser management panel. View AE2 storage and power, GT machines, NEI recipes and AE patterns, submit crafting orders, and chat with in-game players — all from a web browser.\n\nDisabled by default. A server admin must enable the [webConsole] section in config/textech/textech.cfg. Defaults to localhost only (127.0.0.1:8090) with token authentication.
adm.manual.web_console.brief_start_title=Quick Start
adm.manual.web_console.brief_start_text=1. Admin enables [webConsole] enabled=true and restarts the server.\n2. Run /admweb issue in-game to get a token (shown only once).\n3. Open http://127.0.0.1:8090 in a browser and paste the token.\n\nCommon commands: /admweb issue · /admweb revoke · /admweb help\nOP uploads: /admweb recipes upload snapshot (daily) · /admweb recipes upload (full) · /admweb icons upload · /admweb icons import-nesql
adm.manual.web_console.brief_docs_title=Full Documentation
adm.manual.web_console.brief_docs_text=This in-game chapter is a brief introduction only. For the complete user guide (all pages, commands, and security notes), see docs/en/webae/user-guide.md in the mod repository.\n\nAdmins and developers should also see docs/en/webae/developer-guide.md (REST API, network packets, frontend architecture).
adm.manual.web_console.overview_title=Web Console Overview
adm.manual.web_console.overview_text=The WebAE Console is a browser-accessible HTTP management panel embedded in TeXTech. Access at http://127.0.0.1:8090 (by default) using a token obtained via /admweb issue.\n\nCore features:\n- Storage Monitor: real-time AE2 item/fluid type counts, byte usage, and free space.\n- Power Monitor: wireless power/steam levels with input/output rate line charts.\n- GT Machines: online GT machine status, progress bars, and recipe details.\n- Recipe Search: NEI recipe search by output OR input item name with full input/output breakdown.\n- Pattern Manager: view/edit/inject AE2 patterns on ME Interfaces.\n- AE Orders: single or batch crafting orders with real-time progress tracking.\n- Auto-login: stored token reconnects automatically on the next visit.\n- Multi-network: select up to maxNetworksDisplayed networks and toggle Split (per-network cards) / Merged (aggregated totals) display modes.\n- Throttled refresh: the server collects snapshots at refreshIntervalMs (spread across ticks) and the browser polls cache-only; manual refresh is admin-only via /admweb refresh.\n\nRequires the [webConsole] section in config to be enabled. Defaults to localhost-only with token authentication for security.\n\nSee the player guide for detailed usage instructions.
adm.manual.web_console.setup_title=Enable & Configure
adm.manual.web_console.setup_text=The Web Console is disabled by default. To enable, edit config/textech/textech.cfg:\n\n[webConsole]\nenabled=true\nport=8090\nbindAddress=127.0.0.1\nsnapshotIntervalSeconds=30\nrefreshIntervalMs=1000\ngtRefreshIntervalMs=10000\nmaxNetworksDisplayed=5\ntokenLifetimeHours=0\nmaxRecipeCacheMB=64\npowerSampleWindowSeconds=60\ngtDefaultScanRadius=16\nrecipeUploadEnabled=true\n\nRestart the server for changes to take effect.\n\nImportant:\n- bindAddress=127.0.0.1 restricts access to localhost only. Set to 0.0.0.0 for LAN access (use a firewall or SSH tunnel).\n- refreshIntervalMs is the unified refresh interval (ms) for server collection and frontend polling (min 1000, max 60000, default 1000).\n- gtRefreshIntervalMs is the GT machine collection interval (ms, default 10000).\n- maxNetworksDisplayed caps how many AE2 networks the web console can show at once (1-20, default 5).\n- tokenLifetimeHours=0 means tokens never expire; set >0 to enable TTL-based expiry (max 8760).\n- snapshotIntervalSeconds is a legacy fallback used only when refreshIntervalMs is unavailable.
adm.manual.web_console.auth_title=Authentication & Access
adm.manual.web_console.auth_text=The Web Console uses token-based authentication. No Minecraft login credentials are needed.\n\nGetting a token:\n/admweb issue - generates a new token (shown only once — save it immediately)\n/admweb list - lists all issued tokens (OP only, prefix only)\n/admweb revoke [player] - revokes a token (OP can revoke others)\n/adweb refresh [network] - admin-only force snapshot re-collect (Phase 1.2)\n\nBrowser access:\n1. Start the server with webConsole enabled.\n2. Open http://127.0.0.1:8090 (or your server's address) in a browser.\n3. Enter the token from /admweb issue on the login page.\n4. The token is stored in the browser's localStorage (webae_token). With auto-login enabled (default), the console reconnects automatically on your next visit.\n5. If a token is expired or revoked, the login page shows a "token expired" / "token invalid" message and the stored token is cleared so you can re-issue.\n6. To switch tokens later, open Settings → enter a new token → it reconnects immediately.\n\nToken TTL: config tokenLifetimeHours (0 = never expire, >0 = reject after issuedAt + TTL). Tokens persist to config/textech/web-tokens.json (one per player, replaced on re-issue).\n\nAuto-login can be turned off in Settings if you prefer to enter the token manually each visit.
adm.manual.web_console.storage_title=Storage Monitoring
adm.manual.web_console.storage_text=The Storage page provides a real-time overview of your AE2 network storage.\n\nTop overview (Phase 3): configurable widget row reusing the dashboard inheritance system (statCard/progressBar/gauge, data sources, 9-grid alignment, color overrides). Defaults: item types, fluid types, byte usage %, active CPUs. Click Edit overview to drag/add/remove widgets; persisted in localStorage.webae_storage_overview_config. All overview cards are fixed 112px height.\n\nSub-tables: items / fluids / essentia (CPUs moved to the dedicated Crafting CPUs menu). Each sub-table supports column sort and search.\n\nRefresh (Phase 1.2): server collects snapshots every refreshIntervalMs ms, spread across ticks. Browser reads cache only (GET /api/storage); admin force-refresh via POST /api/refresh or /admweb refresh.\n\nMulti-network (Phase 1.4): select networks in the top bar; Split/Merged modes aggregate items/fluids/essentia/bytes.
adm.manual.web_console.cpu_title=Crafting CPUs
adm.manual.web_console.cpu_text=The dedicated Crafting CPUs menu (Hdd icon in sidebar) shows AE2 crafting CPU status.\n\nTop overview (Phase 3): four configurable statCards/progressBars — active/total, total storage usage, total co-processors, parallel crafts; persisted in localStorage.webae_cpu_overview_config.\n\nCPU table: name, status, co-processors, progress, stored items, output, crafting storage, elapsed time. Click a row for a detail Drawer (coordinates, network, storage chart, current task and estimated remaining). Craft history shows \"No history\" until backend support is added.\n\nMulti-network: Merged mode combines all CPUs; Split with multiple networks uses Tabs.\n\nBackend CpuEntry includes crafting-link coordinates, monitor coordinates, remainingItems/startItems, collected by AeSnapshotCollector.
adm.manual.web_console.power_title=Power Monitoring
adm.manual.web_console.power_text=The Power page displays wireless energy network data for both EU and Steam in a configurable GridStack layout (Phase 4).\n\nDefault widgets:\n- EU gauge: current stored energy vs capacity (EU usage %).\n- EU In/Out rate statCards: energy flow (EU/t), calculated via sliding-window sampler.\n- Steam progress bar: steam level vs capacity.\n- Power trend line chart: dual-series SVG chart (EU + steam history, last ~60 samples).\n- Steam In/Out statCards: steam flow rates.\n\nClick **Edit layout** to drag, add, or remove widgets and switch chart types/data sources. Layout persists in the browser (`webae_power_config`). **Power layout settings** adjusts global spacing, colors, and alignment.\n\nMulti-network Split mode uses Tabs to switch per-network snapshots. Auto-refresh updates values silently without unmounting the trend chart.\n\nData uses the same SnapshotScheduler + cache pattern as storage. PowerSampler applies a sliding window for smooth rate readings.
adm.manual.web_console.gt_machines_title=GT Machine Monitoring
adm.manual.web_console.gt_machines_text=The GT Machines page lists all online GregTech machines with their current operational status.\n\nDisplayed per machine:\n- Machine name and type.\n- Current work progress (percentage bar).\n- Active recipe (if any).\n- Power consumption.\n- Input slot items: items currently being consumed.\n- Output slot items: items produced so far.\n\nProgress bars update in real-time during each snapshot interval (gtSnapshotIntervalSeconds).\n\nData is collected via GtMachineStateReader, which accesses GT machine internals through the GtCompat compatibility layer. Requires GTNH GregTech to be installed; the page shows empty otherwise.
adm.manual.web_console.recipes_title=Recipe Search
adm.manual.web_console.recipes_text=The Recipe page supports fuzzy search, item autocomplete, infinite-scroll recipe overview, compact/detailed layouts, and full/merged display mode (Phase 5).\n\nCollection & upload:\n1. Client hybrid collect: NeiRecipeCollector (main thread, NEI/AE2, etc.) + GameRecipeCollector (vanilla/GT supplement).\n2. Handler labels are localized on the client, e.g. Alloy Smelter (gt.recipe.alloysmelter); item itemId includes meta for icon cache alignment.\n3. Merged single-session upload via PacketWebRecipeUpload; RecipeUploadSession ensures only the first isStart clears server memory.\n4. Server RecipeCacheStore keeps output/input indexes plus handlerRecipeKeys/suggestPrefixIndex; gzip persistence to config/textech/web-recipes.json.gz.\n5. Client RecipeLocalExporter also writes .minecraft/TeXTechWebAE/web-recipes.json.gz (same gzip schema).\n\nUsage:\n- Overview loads automatically; scroll down to fetch more (24 per batch).\n- Default fuzzy search by item name; picking a suggestion searches by output registry.\n- Category area: multi-select handler Tags, search handler names, collapse/expand; compact cards are square and open a detail modal on click.\n- Merged mode groups by primary output; multiple recipe types for the same item switch via modal Tabs.\n- Detailed layout uses independent CSS Grid columns; click an item for Craft / Usage tabs.\n\nAn OP must run /admweb recipes upload snapshot (daily) or upload (full) in-game before the web UI has data (Phase 2 removed the in-game keybind; upload is command-only); re-upload after handler label or itemId changes.
adm.manual.web_console.patterns_title=Pattern Management
adm.manual.web_console.patterns_text=The Pattern page provides a full AE2 pattern management interface through the browser (Extended Pattern Terminal style).\n\nFeatures:\n- Pattern overview: lists all patterns on ME Interface slots across the network; search, multi-select, batch delete/export.\n- Editor: 9×3 input grid and output rows show item icons and stack sizes; outputs support ×2/×4/×8/×16/×32/×64 scaling and ÷2 (never below original recipe amount).\n- Recipe search: merged by primary output; click to add the default recipe or open Details to pick a recipe type.\n- Encode: PatternEncoder builds AE2 NBT; with consumeBlank, BlankPatternHelper deducts 1 blank pattern from the AE network (NO_BLANK_PATTERN when insufficient).\n- Inject: PatternInjector writes the encoded pattern to a target ME Interface; interface list shows coords, pattern count, machine recipe type, and existing pattern details.\n\nAll network-modifying operations run on the main thread via CountDownLatch (5s timeout).
adm.manual.web_console.orders_title=AE Crafting Orders
adm.manual.web_console.orders_text=The Orders page lets you submit AE2 crafting jobs directly from the browser.\n\nCPU selection:\n- A top dropdown lists all crafting CPUs on the network (name, capacity, parallelism, busy/idle).\n- Leave as "Auto assign" for AE2 to pick a CPU; specify a name to target that CPU.\n\nOrder by pattern (tab):\n- GET /api/patterns/browse paginated dual-source (Grid + Interface), debounced search, infinite scroll on reach bottom.\n- View toggle: virtual-scrolled "By product" cards or "By pattern" list for large networks.\n- Grid/Interface tags show source; detail modal lazy-fetches full I/O for Grid entries.\n- Multi-select patterns, set quantity, batch-submit to /api/order/batch.\n\nOrder by item (tab):\n- Search AE storage, enter quantity, submit to /api/order.\n- Or add multiple rows and submit /api/order/batch at once.\n\nCraft tree (tab):\n- Enter item registry name and quantity; GET /api/craft/tree recursively expands NEI recipe chain.\n- Table shows required / in-storage / missing per level; leaf nodes are raw materials.\n\nOrder tracking:\n- Active and history orders come from GET /api/order/list (history field).\n- Auto-refreshes every 3s; hybrid progress: AE2 calculation phase → real CPU progress → time estimate fallback.\n- Completed jobs move to history at 100%; history shows CPU name with tooltip for co-proc/storage/parallel details.\n- "Cancel all" calls POST /api/order/cancel.\n\nBackend: AssistantServerServices.submitCraft accepts cpuName; OrderHandler keeps in-memory historyOrders (max 200, cleared on restart).\n\nNote: order submission blocks the HTTP thread until the main thread finishes (CountDownLatch, 15s timeout).
adm.manual.web_console.theme_dashboard_title=Themes & Dashboard Customization
adm.manual.web_console.theme_dashboard_text=Phase 2 added a full theme system and a customizable drag-and-drop dashboard.\n\nTheme system:\n- Theme = color scheme x layout preset, chosen independently in Settings.\n- Color schemes (24): 19 classic + 5 Phase 8 sci-fi themes (hologram/plasma/neon-pulse/quantum/crystal). Each recolors the background, accent, text, and status colors.\n- Layout presets (5): standard, compact (denser, smaller fonts), wide (larger gaps, bigger fonts), sidebar-right (sidebar on the right), topnav (sidebar hidden, navigation moved into the top bar).\n- Your choice persists in the browser (localStorage webae_theme as "color|layout"); legacy dark/light choices auto-migrate.\n- Charts recolor automatically when you switch themes.\n\nDashboard customization:\n- The Dashboard tab is a GridStack.js grid you can edit: drag widgets by their handle, resize from the corner, and use the toolbar to toggle Edit mode.\n- Add Widget opens a library of widget types: stat card, progress bar (horizontal/vertical/circular), line chart, bar chart, pie chart, data table, gauge.\n- Each widget binds to a data source (item types, fluid types, EU stored, bytes usage %, power history, top items, network compare, etc.) and a scope: global (aggregated across all selected networks) or per-network (bound to one network; in split mode each network gets its own copy).\n- Edit a widget to change its type, data source, scope, style (progress orientation, time window, max rows), and size.\n- Layout persists in localStorage.webae_dashboard_config. "Reset Layout" restores the default widget set.\n- Global style defaults and widgets JSON import/export are covered in the Dashboard Settings chapter.\n- In split multi-network mode, global widgets appear in a top "Overview" grid and per-network widgets repeat under each network's section.
adm.manual.web_console.topology_title=Network Topology
adm.manual.web_console.topology_text=Web console includes a Network Topology page (sidebar: Network Topology) backed by a simulated AE API.\n\nFeatures:\n- Does not reflect real AE cable routing; only counts devices on the grid and groups them by rules.\n- Logical view: aggregate by device class (controller/drive/interface/CPU/P2P/quantum/misc) with star fake cables radiating from the controller hub.\n- Spatial view: coarse clustering by dimension + 64x64 chunk bins — still not physical topology.\n- P2P channels view: list P2P tunnels grouped by frequency (not physical links), with endpoint coords and IN/OUT side.\n- Fake cables show simulated channel usage (e.g. 12/32); when the AE API is readable, meta also includes real channel totals.\n- SVG graph with pan/zoom; click a node to list device coordinates; CSV export on the topology page.\n\nAPI: GET /api/network/topology?network=<id>&mode=logical|spatial; GET /api/network/p2p?network=<id> (P2P map).\n\nConfig ([webConsole]): topologyEnabled (default true), topologyCacheTtlMs (default 30000 ms).
