adm.manual.web_console.icon_cache_title=Item Icons & Texture Packs
adm.manual.web_console.icon_cache_text=Phase 3 added an item/fluid icon cache so the web console shows real game icons instead of plain text.\n\nWorkflow:\n1. An OP runs /admweb icons upload [packName] in-game to trigger rendering (Phase 2 removed the in-game keybind; upload is command-only now).\n2. The client IconRenderer (@SideOnly CLIENT) iterates Item.itemRegistry, renders each item to a 32x32 PNG with RenderItem + an offscreen Framebuffer, a few items per frame to avoid lag.\n3. Finished icons are packed into an IconBundle (itemId -> base64 PNG) and uploaded in chunks via PacketWebIconUpload (network ID 28).\n4. The server decodes each entry and writes it to config/textech/web-icons/<packName>/<itemId>.png, then refreshes the IconStore index.\n5. Progress is acknowledged via PacketWebIconUploadAck (network ID 29).\n\nWeb usage:\n- Item tables and recipe inputs/outputs show real icons; failed icons fall back to a name abbreviation.\n- Settings page has a texture-pack selector (persisted in localStorage webae_icon_pack); switching reloads every icon with a ?v=<timestamp> cache-buster.\n- Admins (OP>=2) can upload a texture-pack zip in Settings (POST /api/icon/pack?pack=<name>); the server extracts it with Zip Slip path-traversal protection.\n- You can also fetch icons directly via /icons/<pack>/<itemId>.png (WebConsoleServer serves the external config/textech/web-icons/ directory).\n\nConfig ([webConsole] section): iconCacheEnabled, iconUploadEnabled, iconPackEnabled, nesqlRepositoryPath (import-nesql; empty = TeXTechWebAE), iconMissingDispatchPerTick. /api/config returns the boolean flags.\n\nCommands: /admweb icons upload [packName], /admweb icons import-nesql [pack] [subpath] (defaults to TeXTechWebAE), /admweb icons status.\n\nLazy-load: 404 icons enqueue IconMissingQueue; when ready the server emits SSE icon-ready and the frontend refreshes icons via webae-icon-ready.
adm.manual.web_console.recipe_cache_title=Recipe Cache Optimization
adm.manual.web_console.recipe_cache_text=Phase 3 made incremental improvements to the recipe cache (search and inverted indexes were already done in Phase 1 and are not redone here). NEI performance Phase 0–4 added handlerRecipeKeys/suggestPrefixIndex, recipeCacheMode=full (GTNH default; lru evicts when maxRecipeCacheMB exceeded), RecipeUploadThrottler (recipeUploadBatchesPerTick), and RecipeSearchRateLimiter (recipeSearchMinIntervalMs).\n\nDisk persistence:\n- RecipeCacheStore.ingest() now auto-saves to disk asynchronously via HandlerTick.enqueueServerTask (debounced: only one save is queued at a time, so not every batch triggers a write).\n- The save format is now gzip-compressed: config/textech/web-recipes.json.gz, which is much smaller. On load the gzip file is preferred; if an old uncompressed web-recipes.json exists it is read first and migrated to gzip on the next save.\n- Client local copy: .minecraft/TeXTechWebAE/web-recipes.json.gz (RecipeLocalExporter; written with upload commands).\n- lastDiskSave (last save timestamp) and diskCacheSize (gzip file size in bytes) are tracked for status queries.\n\nStatus:\n- /api/recipes/status now includes diskCacheSize and lastDiskSave.\n- The frontend Recipes tab shows disk cache size and last-save time, with a "re-export" hint.\n- /admweb recipes status prints the same disk-cache information.\n\nCommands:\n- /admweb recipes upload [snapshot|deep] — upload NEI recipes (snapshot = storage items only; deep = full item scan); also writes client TeXTechWebAE/web-recipes.json.gz.\n- /admweb recipes export — alias of upload.\n- /admweb recipes status — view cache status (including disk cache).\n- /admweb recipes clear — clear memory and disk cache (OP only).
adm.manual.web_console.safety_title=Security & Safety
adm.manual.web_console.safety_text=The Web Console is a powerful tool — treat its access credentials with care.\n\nSecurity features:\n- Token authentication (random UUID per player, persisted to config/textech/web-tokens.json; re-issue replaces the previous token).\n- All /api/ endpoints enforce Bearer authentication (no opt-out config).\n- Admin-only endpoints (POST /api/refresh, /api/refresh/batch, /api/power/refresh, /api/gt/machines/refresh) additionally require OP level >= 2.\n- Default localhost-only binding (127.0.0.1).\n- No TLS — NanoHTTPD does not support HTTPS.\n\nSafety recommendations:\n- Never set bindAddress=0.0.0.0 on a public-facing server without a firewall or reverse proxy.\n- Use SSH tunneling (ssh -L 8090:localhost:8090 user@server) for remote access instead of opening the port.\n- For LAN parties, share tokens only with trusted players.\n- Revoke tokens (/admweb revoke) immediately if compromised.\n- Tokens grant full read/write access to AE2 storage and crafting — guard them like server passwords.\n\nConfiguration validation:\n- enabled is false by default (opt-in).\n- bindAddress defaults to 127.0.0.1 (not 0.0.0.0).\n- tokenLifetimeHours defaults to 0 (never expire); set >0 to enable TTL-based expiry.\n- refreshIntervalMs / gtRefreshIntervalMs are clamped to 1000-60000 ms.\n- maxNetworksDisplayed is clamped to 1-20.

# ===== Web Console Manual: New Pages (Phase E + upgrades) =====
adm.manual.web_console.command_upload_title=Command-Triggered Upload
adm.manual.web_console.command_upload_text=OP players trigger recipe and icon uploads via chat commands (Phase 2 removed the in-game keybind, so upload is command-only).\n\nCommands:\n- /admweb recipes upload [snapshot|deep] — upload NEI recipes (snapshot = storage items only; deep = full item scan); also writes client TeXTechWebAE/web-recipes.json.gz.\n- /admweb icons upload [packName] — same trigger packet; client renders item icons and uploads via PacketWebIconUpload.\n- /admweb icons import-nesql [pack] [subpath] — import pre-rendered PNGs from nesqlRepositoryPath (empty = TeXTechWebAE; incremental).\n\nBoth upload sub-commands require OP (canUseOpCommands); base /admweb permission level stays 0.\n\nClient collection runs on the main thread (Minecraft.addScheduledTask) because NEI APIs are not thread-safe; RecipeUploadThrottler sends recipeUploadBatchesPerTick batches per tick.\n\nDebug logging: set [debug] debugWebae=true to print handler counts, total numRecipes, and filtered recipe counts during collection.
adm.manual.web_console.refresh_status_title=Top Bar Refresh Status
adm.manual.web_console.refresh_status_text=The auto-refresh countdown no longer toggles a separate text element on and off (which caused the top bar to shift width).\n\n- A fixed-width status span (min-width 90px) sits next to the green connection dot and is always rendered.\n- The status text follows a small state machine: "Idle" / "Ns until refresh" / "Refreshing...".\n- The refresh button's spinner is absolutely positioned as an overlay so the button width never changes during loading.\n\nThis removes the flex reflow jitter that used to happen every refresh cycle.
adm.manual.web_console.dashboard_settings_title=Dashboard Settings Panel
adm.manual.web_console.dashboard_settings_text=Besides per-widget editing, the dashboard has a global settings drawer for defaults and presets.\n\nOpen it from the Dashboard / Storage overview / Power toolbar "Settings" button. The drawer uses Tabs:\n- **Layout**: page margin, widget gap, content inset (visual padding without changing GridStack snap), default 9-grid alignment.\n- **Chart**: default font/chart ratio, line chart stretch mode (fit / stretchX / fill), Y/time axis toggles, optional footer "updated Ns ago".\n- **Colors**: five default colors + color preset management.\n- **Advanced**: export/import widgets JSON (clipboard); color presets.\n\nThe per-widget edit dialog also uses Tabs (Basic / Layout / Colors / Advanced) with overrides for contentInset, chartStretchMode, border width, statCard showDelta and significant digits.\n\nAll three GridStack pages (main dashboard, storage overview, power) share WidgetShell styling (CSS variables); edit mode supports copy widget.\n\nPersistence: main dashboard uses localStorage.webae_dashboard_config; storage/power pages have their own keys. Older saved configs merge with defaults for new fields.
adm.manual.web_console.sidebar_modes_title=Sidebar Three-State Toggle
adm.manual.web_console.sidebar_modes_text=The sidebar collapse button at the bottom was removed. Instead, a small tab-shaped toggle sits on the sidebar edge and cycles through three modes:\n- expanded (default) — full sidebar with icons and labels.\n- collapsed — 60px wide, icons only, labels hidden.\n- hidden — sidebar slides out of view (translateX -100%); only the toggle button remains visible so you can bring it back.\n\nThe active mode is stored on aside.sidebar via a data-mode attribute and drives all CSS transitions. In the sidebar-right layout the toggle moves to the left edge and the hidden direction reverses. The choice persists in localStorage (webae_sidebar_mode).\n\nThe mobile slide-in (sidebarMobileOpen) stays a separate control so narrow screens keep their own behavior.
adm.manual.web_console.chat_title=Web Chat
adm.manual.web_console.chat_text=The web console has a Chat tab (the message icon in the sidebar and topnav) that bridges browser and in-game chat.\n\nLayout:\n- Left: player list with avatar, name, online duration, and last-seen time. Online players are listed first.\n- Right: bubble-style message area with avatar, sender name, source tag (Web/Game/System), timestamp, and content. Messages from the web are shown on the right, others on the left (heuristic by source==='web'). System messages render as centered yellow pills.\n- Bottom: input box (Enter to send).\n\nSending: POST /api/chat/send with {content} reads your playerUuid from the token, appends a source=web message to ChatMessageStore, and broadcasts it in-game as "[Web] <name>: content". Banned players and empty/over-long content are rejected.\n\nPolling: while the Chat tab is active, the client polls GET /api/chat/since=<ts> every 2.5s and refreshes the player list via GET /api/players every 10s.\n\nAvatars: the server resolves each player's skin URL from their GameProfile textures property (base64-decoded) and returns it as skinUrl. The browser loads https://textures.minecraft.net/<hash> at 32x32; offline players or failed loads fall back to a circular first-letter placeholder.\n\nHistory: GET /api/chat/history?limit=200&since=<ts> returns recent messages; the store keeps a 200-entry ring buffer and persists to config/textech/web-chat.json (debounced) so history survives restarts.\n\nSettings: showAvatars / showPlayerInfo toggles persist in localStorage (webae_chat_settings).
adm.manual.web_console.reload_command_title=Reload Command
adm.manual.web_console.reload_command_text=/admweb reload now actually reloads the TeXTech configuration instead of only printing a hint.\n\nIt calls Config.reloadConfiguration(), which re-reads the active config file (config/textech/textech.cfg) and re-runs every section loader (debug, compat, ai, voice, assistant, plannerHud, dataLoom, superOrange, matterBallDecompressor, grapple, webConsole).\n\nNotes:\n- Some options still need a server restart to take effect (for example enabled, port, bindAddress for the web server itself). The command response lists this caveat.\n- Token and runtime data files (web-tokens.json, web-players.json, web-chat.json, web-icons/) are not touched by reload.

